<decision #track.add-eidolon-natural-language-workflow-authoring.actor-boundary apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91C>
  Who owns semantic generation and who owns resource writes?
  </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91C>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91D>
    Eidolon actor generates; WorkflowComponent validates and writes.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91D>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91E>
    The coordinator delegates semantic authoring to an Eidolon child actor, which may mutate resources only through native workflow tools.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91E>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91F>
    This prevents both a deterministic heuristic pretending to be AI authoring and an actor bypassing resource authority.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91F>
  )>
)>

<decision #track.add-eidolon-natural-language-workflow-authoring.cli-runtime apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { status = "accepted" priority = "P0" } (
  <question ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91G>
  How does the workflow CLI obtain AI generation?
  </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91G>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91H>
    Invoke the in-process Eidolon headless runtime.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91H>
    <decision-text ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91J>
    CLI create/edit runs an Eidolon turn that routes to WorkflowAuthor; it never spawns an external agent executable.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91J>
    <rationale ?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91K>
    Eidolon already is the AI runtime and should remain the only provider/session authority.
    </?01M05F1PQC3VV6GQAZCAW0B91K>
  )>
)>
